  "body": "Boutique living for the young at heart. Being 65+ years has its advantages with modern, easy living in the heart of Orewa.\r\n\r\nIf you are looking for a stunning one-bedroom apartment offering you sunshine and light, plenty of space, good storage and roomy enough for one or two people to live comfortably, then this is the apartment for you.\r\nThe open plan lounge / dining area has a huge feeling of space - extended further with the glassed-in conservatory where you can sit and relax and enjoy the sunsets from. Beautiful! The conservatory can be opened up on bluebird days to let the fresh air in, or on the windier days when it’s still sunny – you can sit and read while staying warm inside.\r\n\r\nThis ground floor apartment opens out to a courtyard - so makes it ideal for small pets if you have a cat or dog.  The kitchen is a pleasure to cook in with plenty of drawers, cupboards, pantry, dish-drawer, waste disposal and wall oven. All you have to bring is your microwave and fridge. There are high quality Bosch appliances including a washing machine and dryer in the hide-a-way laundry area.\r\n\r\nThis apartment has a large master bedroom, giving you space for furniture. The walk-in wardrobe gives you plenty of room for your clothes and connects to the large dual access en-suite bathroom.\r\n\r\nOffering an unparalleled lifestyle opportunity; everything you could wish for is here - summer beach days with visiting family, take a walk along the estuary pathway and enjoy a coffee at one of the many cafes or an evening meal with friends at one of the local restaurants. Feeling adventurous? take a drive to nearby Matakana, Snells Beach or picturesque Tawharanui Regional Park.\r\n\r\nContact Lance to arrange a private viewing and discover the lifestyle you’ve always wanted.\r\n\r\nPurchase is under a Licence to Occupy Agreement",
